 {
  "coord": "15:30",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "'Question:' is Benedick answering Beatrice, not asking her something.",
  "replacement": "BENEDICK. Good question. Why, an hour of noise and a quarter of an hour of tears. So it's most sensible for a wise man—if Don Worm, his conscience, sees no objection—to be the trumpet of his own virtues, as I am for myself. That's enough about praising myself, who, I'll testify myself, deserve praise. And now tell me, how is your cousin?"
 },
